From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] passes: real test modules for
 loop_analysis/resolve_asm/univsr; fix 2 wrong-code bugs; wire univsr

Test modules (34 new unit tests, all green):
* loop_analysis (11): BlockBitSet across word boundaries, DominanceChecker
  incl. diamonds/disconnected components/out-of-bounds, self loops,
  preheader vs dedicated preheader, multi-latch merging, nested loops +
  subloop relation, LoopNest hierarchy/depths/traversals, loop RPO,
  degenerate CFGs, and irreducible cycles (must NOT be natural loops).
  Uses the canonical FlatAdj::from_vecs_usize test constructor - PR #59's
  version invented FlatAdj fields that never existed.
* resolve_asm (11): GEP/Add/Sub/Cast/Copy chains, commuted adds, negative
  and zero offsets, Shl-scaled offsets, constraint filtering, preservation
  of preset symbols, cross-block def chains, fast-path no-op.
* univsr (12): stride 1/4 reversion, SIB-scale rejection, transitive GEP
  displacement preservation, per-block Shl CSE, span/instruction sync, and
  five soundness rejections (below).

univsr soundness (pass was silently unsound AND dead code - GLM's audit
missed both):
* index IV is now verified to be a canonical counter (init==0, step==+1);
  any other (init,step) silently addressed the wrong element
* escape validation is now a strict whitelist over ALL instructions and
  terminators, tracking the full derived-pointer set; previously the
  increment GEP's uses were never checked, so `for (p=a; p!=end; p++)`
  exit conditions would have compared Copy(base) - an infinite loop
* wired into the pipeline (x86-64 only, after IVSR, CCC_NO_UNIVSR /
  CCC_DISABLE_PASSES=univsr escape hatches, LCCC_DEBUG_UNIVSR tracing);
  the pass had never been invoked from anywhere

Wrong-code fixes (GLM audit items BUG-1/BUG-2, both verified):
* usual_arithmetic_conversion: when the signed type has higher rank but
  the same width (LL vs UL on LP64, L vs UI on ILP32), the result is now
  the unsigned counterpart per C11 6.3.1.8. Frontend/_Generic/enum-init
  now match GCC (was: `_Generic(ll+ul)` -> "ll", enum arm -> 0).
  New regression test usual_arith_conversion.c diffs against GCC.
* __builtin_cpu_supports: folded 1 for EVERY feature except avx512*
  (including AMX/XOP/SSE4A the target lacks -> guaranteed SIGILL in
  runtime dispatchers). Now folds from an exact Raptor-Lake allowlist;
  unknown features fold to 0, the safe direction for dispatch fallbacks.

Also: CallInfo and IrType gain Default (test ergonomics; Void is the
IrType default). 641 lib tests, 152 regressions, all green.
