Subject: [PATCH 2/3] x86 assembler: fix pextrw memory-destination encoding;
 add thin-LTO release profile

pextrw mem fix (GLM audit BUG-4, verified): the legacy 66 0F C5 form is
REGISTER-ONLY per the Intel SDM; emitting it with a memory ModRM silently
encoded a different instruction. Memory destinations now transparently
switch to the SSE4.1 form 66 0F 3A 15 /r ib. Verified byte-identical to
GNU as for reg, mem, and REX-extended (xmm9) forms.

Cargo.toml gains [profile.release] with lto = "thin". Deliberately NOT
panic = "abort" (GLM's suggestion): compiler_main() reports worker-thread
panics as proper "internal error" diagnostics via join()+downcast, which
abort would destroy. Research builds still pin opt-level=1 via env.

641 lib tests, 153 regressions, 86 linker tests - all green.
